# cover_high_divide_dusk: the cover plate, the High Divide at dusk.
# Mount Olympus takes the last light across the Hoh valley; the first stars
# are out; a hiker in a rust jacket walks the crest trail among subalpine
# firs and pink heather. A tall plate (160x320, doc 11.2), drawn in its own
# dusk colors, so it shows with the day (identity) table. The top 95 rows
# are quiet navy sky for the title. No gold anywhere (BUILD_PLAN 4.1).
#
# We look south from the Divide. The sun has just set behind our right
# shoulder (west, northwest), so every face that turns right or toward us
# is lit and every face that turns left (east) is in shadow: on the
# mountains and on each fir. Only the summits still stand above the
# earth's shadow, so they glow pink; the snow below them is white, and
# lower still the massif has gone glacier blue. The lower ranges, already
# in shadow, stand dark against the last pink of the sky.
#
# How the shapes are drawn: each shape's outline in its own color, then a
# fill from a seed inside (AGI style, so the draw-in shows lines, then the
# fills flooding in). A shape cut out of a bigger one gets its boundary
# line, then the fill. A dithered seam sits between a line of the color
# above and a line of the color below; where the upper line has to be a
# wall first, it is drawn in ink and then redrawn in its own color.
@ sky
# Night navy, through slate, to the pink glow low in the west. Each band
# is cut by an ink row; the band's fill then takes that row too. The sky
# stops at row 172, below the lowest point of the skyline, so the draw-in
# never floods pink over the ground before the ground is drawn.
C 0  L 0,96 159,96  L 0,104 159,104  L 0,112 159,112  L 0,120 159,120
     L 0,126 159,126  L 0,132 159,132  L 0,138 159,138  L 0,144 159,144
     L 0,172 159,172
